	(descr "OPSCO SK6812-EC20 addressable RGB LED (LCSC C2909058), 2.0 x 2.0 x 0.65 mm, 4-pad SMD, TOP mount. AUTHORED 2026-10-12 from the manufacturer drawing: Guangdong OPSCO SK6812-EC20-001 Rev. A/2 (sending date 2026-03-24), mirrored at studio/press/references/components/sk6812-ec20-datasheet.pdf, retrieved 2026-10-12 from the datasheet link on jlcpcb.com/partdetail/C2909058 (https://wmsc.lcsc.com/wmsc/upload/file/pdf/v2/lcsc/2110250930_OPSCO-Optoelectronics-SK6812-EC20_C2909058.pdf). PADS are section 6 'PCB recommended pad size' (PDF page 5, top view): 0.8 (x) by 0.7 (y) on a 0.5 mm gap both ways, so centres at x +/-0.65, y +/-0.6 and the land is 2.1 x 1.9. PINS are section 5 (PDF page 4) placed as the section 6 top view draws them: 1 VDD bottom-right, 2 DOUT top-right, 3 GND top-left, 4 DIN bottom-left (KiCad +y down), so pad N is the manufacturer's pin N and the order runs counterclockwise from pin 1; the section 4 bottom view is the mirror of this and agrees. BODY is section 4: 2.0 x 2.0 x 0.65, tolerance +/-0.1 (section 4 note 2), so F.Fab is +/-1.0. ORIGIN is the body centre, which is the functional datum (the emitting area): the land is symmetric about it on both axes and section 4's top view places the R/G/B dice near the centre line; the die positions are not dimensioned, so the emitter-at-centre rests on symmetry. PIN 1 is marked twice: the F.Fab body chamfer at the pad-1 corner and an F.SilkS L bracket outside pad 1 (0.15 mm line, JLCPCB's minimum; 0.175 mm from pad copper). UNSOURCED: courtyard (+/-1.3 x +/-1.2, land + 0.25), silk bracket, chamfer size. No text on F.SilkS: a legal glyph is larger than the part.")
	(tags "LED RGB addressable SK6812 EC20 2020 C2909058")
